WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.589
You signed the trust.

2
00:00:02.589 --> 00:00:03.528
Great.

3
00:00:03.528 --> 00:00:08.100
But a trust only controls what is in it.

4
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.085
One.

5
00:00:09.085 --> 00:00:10.287
Your home.

6
00:00:10.287 --> 00:00:12.925
This usually means a new deed,

7
00:00:12.925 --> 00:00:17.600
recorded in the county where the property sits.

8
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:18.511
Two.

9
00:00:18.511 --> 00:00:19.832
Bank accounts.

10
00:00:19.832 --> 00:00:22.205
Many banks retitle the account,

11
00:00:22.205 --> 00:00:24.578
or add a payable-on-death name,

12
00:00:24.578 --> 00:00:27.100
depending on the plan.

13
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:28.173
Three.

14
00:00:28.173 --> 00:00:29.881
Brokerage accounts.

15
00:00:29.881 --> 00:00:35.100
Typically you retitle them to the trust with your broker.

16
00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:36.014
Four.

17
00:00:36.014 --> 00:00:37.563
Retirement accounts.

18
00:00:37.563 --> 00:00:40.275
These usually stay out of the trust.

19
00:00:40.275 --> 00:00:43.042
You name the beneficiary on the form.

20
00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:45.061
Ask before changing anything,

21
00:00:45.061 --> 00:00:47.100
because of taxes.

22
00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:48.080
Five.

23
00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.480
Life insurance.

24
00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.823
Review who is the beneficiary,

25
00:00:51.823 --> 00:00:55.100
and whether the trust should be.

26
00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:55.970
Six.

27
00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.339
Everything else, like furniture,

28
00:00:58.339 --> 00:01:00.285
jewelry, and keepsakes.

29
00:01:00.285 --> 00:01:04.100
A short assignment document can cover these.

30
00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.182
Our checklist tracks all six.

31
00:01:07.182 --> 00:01:12.100
Download it and bring it to your next meeting.
